# One request per endpoint. VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request".
@base = http://localhost:5080

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### API reference (Development): open http://localhost:5080/scalar in a browser
GET {{base}}/openapi/v1.json

### Venue and booking rules
GET {{base}}/api/venue

### Resources (courts, rooms) with opening hours
GET {{base}}/api/resources

### Slots for one venue-local day (yyyy-MM-dd). Leave out date for today. Slots are free, booked, past or closed;
### "closures" lists closures (holidays, maintenance) touching the day. Booking into one is 422 resource_closed.
GET {{base}}/api/resources/court-1/availability?date=2026-10-20

### Book: "start" is a slot's "start" from availability (UTC). A bk-customer cookie is issued on first call.
### This makes a hold: status "pending" with "holdExpiresAt" (10 minutes, Holds:Minutes). The slot is taken until
### the hold is confirmed, released (cancel), or expires; then it is free again by itself.
# @name hold
POST {{base}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceId": "court-1", "start": "2026-10-20T01:00:00Z", "slots": 1, "name": "Nam" }

### Pay the deposit and confirm the hold above before it expires (409 hold_expired after). Confirming twice is harmless.
### Fake provider tokens: tok_visa (approved), tok_declined / tok_insufficient_funds / tok_expired_card (402, the hold
### stays), tok_unavailable (503, nothing charged), tok_timeout (503, charged but the answer was lost: send it again,
### it cannot charge twice). The deposit is in GET /api/venue ("deposit") and on each booking ("deposit").
POST {{base}}/api/bookings/{{hold.response.body.id}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentToken": "tok_visa" }

### Payment webhooks are signed by the provider, so send them with: node tools/payment-webhook.mjs <type> <paymentId>
### (payment.succeeded, payment.failed, refund.succeeded; --event evt_1 twice to see "duplicate"; --bad-signature for 401)

### My bookings
GET {{base}}/api/bookings/mine

### One booking (paste an id)
GET {{base}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Cancel (paste an id)
POST {{base}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel

### --- Accounts. The session is the HttpOnly "bk-auth" cookie; REST Client keeps cookies between requests. ---

### Sign up (signs in too). Bookings made before on this client move to the account: see "movedBookings".
POST {{base}}/api/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nam@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery", "name": "Nam" }

### Sign in
POST {{base}}/api/account/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nam@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery" }

### Who am I (401 unauthenticated when signed out)
GET {{base}}/api/me

### Sign out
POST {{base}}/api/account/signout

### --- Staff (Staff or Admin role). To make your account staff in development, add your email to
### Accounts:Bootstrap:Staff in src/BookingApp.Api/appsettings.Development.json, restart, and sign in again.

### The day schedule: every resource, every booking (any status) with the actions allowed now, and closures
GET {{base}}/api/staff/schedule?date=2026-10-20

### Mark a booking completed / a no-show (only once it has started). Paste an id from the schedule.
POST {{base}}/api/staff/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/no-show

### Cancel any booking that has not ended, with a reason the customer sees
POST {{base}}/api/staff/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Court flooded" }

### Block time for maintenance (refused with 409 bookings_in_the_way if confirmed bookings overlap)
POST {{base}}/api/staff/closures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceId": "court-1", "start": "2026-10-20T07:00:00Z", "end": "2026-10-20T08:00:00Z", "reason": "Net repair" }

### --- Admin (Admin role). In development: add your email to Accounts:Bootstrap:Admin, restart, sign in again.
### Every change below is recorded in the audit log with your account.

### Change a court's weekly opening hours (days left out are closed)
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/resources/court-1/hours
Content-Type: application/json

{ "hours": [
  { "day": "monday", "open": "08:00", "close": "20:00" }, { "day": "tuesday", "open": "08:00", "close": "20:00" },
  { "day": "wednesday", "open": "08:00", "close": "20:00" }, { "day": "thursday", "open": "08:00", "close": "20:00" },
  { "day": "friday", "open": "08:00", "close": "20:00" }, { "day": "saturday", "open": "09:00", "close": "18:00" },
  { "day": "sunday", "open": "09:00", "close": "18:00" } ] }

### Add a resource (closed until its hours are set)
POST {{base}}/api/admin/resources
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "court-3", "name": "Tennis court 3", "kind": "court", "capacity": 4, "slotMinutes": 60, "maxSlotsPerBooking": 2 }

### A holiday: close every resource for whole days (leave out resourceId)
POST {{base}}/api/admin/closures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "2026-12-25", "to": "2026-12-26", "reason": "Christmas" }

### Closures in a date range
GET {{base}}/api/admin/closures?from=2026-12-01&to=2026-12-31

### The booking rules, and changing them
GET {{base}}/api/admin/policy

###
PUT {{base}}/api/admin/policy
Content-Type: application/json

{ "maxDaysAhead": 30, "minLeadMinutes": 15, "cancellationCutoffHours": 2, "maxActiveBookingsPerCustomer": 5 }

### The audit log: who changed what (newest first)
GET {{base}}/api/admin/audit?take=20

### --- Idempotent booking: send the same Idempotency-Key twice. The second answer is the first one again
### (header Idempotency-Replayed: true), and only one booking exists. Use a new key for a new booking.
POST {{base}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 6f1c0d2e-3a5b-4c7d-9e8f-0a1b2c3d4e5f

{ "resourceId": "court-2", "start": "2026-10-20T03:00:00Z", "slots": 1, "name": "Retry test" }
